---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About">
  <header class="article-head"><h1>About this journal</h1></header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Most writing about AI is about models and chips. This journal covers one thing underneath them: power for AI data centres. It follows the power from the grid connection through the transformers, the turbines and the reactors, into the building and out through the cooling, and asks at each step what decides whether it arrives on time.</p>
    <p>That layer is where the physics is slow, the data is public, and the constraint is real. It is also the part that almost nobody explains in plain language.</p>
    <p>Each piece here starts with a one-line version anyone can understand, then goes as deep as the subject needs. Where I have a view, I say what would prove it wrong. The plain English comes first, and a section for investors follows on the same page, with the numbers, the claims on record and what would prove them wrong.</p>
    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>I'm {SITE.author}, a civil engineer by training (UCL MEng, 2025) who moved into investment research. I spent time as an Investment Analyst at Cross Labs / Cross Compass in Tokyo, and I now run this journal as Founder and Research Analyst, The Physical Layer, publishing research on power for AI data centres.</p>
    <p>Engineering taught me to respect what physically has to be true. Research taught me to say what I think will happen, and what would prove me wrong. This journal is where the two meet.</p>
    <p class="sources">Everything here is personal research, not investment advice. Reach me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or on <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
